{
  "_comment": [
    "THE TESTBED MAP (LANDSCAPE.md §7.1). This file is CONTENT: it says where",
    "this game's things are. It does not say how a world scales — that is the",
    "engine's mechanism and deliberately is not here.",
    "",
    "Two conventions matter and both exist to avoid baking an anchor:",
    "  * crag.rockline_frac / treeline_frac are FRACTIONS of the summit, not",
    "    metres. The summit is a NUMBERS row (L0_RELIEF), so writing 74.75 here",
    "    would silently unpin the splat and tree lines the day that row moves.",
    "  * carves.crag_tunnel waypoints are in SURVEY SPACE — the elevations and",
    "    positions as they were surveyed against a 52 m Ravenscar. The engine",
    "    applies the ascent and footprint scaling. Same reason: the climb has to",
    "    grow with the summit or the tunnel buries itself, and a scaled copy",
    "    written out here would stop growing.",
    "Absent keys keep the engine's neutral value; the engine holds NO map."
  ],

